        "CharitablePurpose": "New Zealand Red Cross' mission is to improve the lives of vulnerable people by mobilizing the power of humanity and enhancing community resilience.\r\nWe aim to achieve our mission through the delivery of our three core services pillars - Migration, International and Emergency Management - and through other community services.",
        "EntityStructure": "Members make up our local Branches and groups, who also join to form Area Councils.  Area Councils have representatives at National Council where the National Board is elected to governs our organisation. Members of the National Board are elected or co-opted to provide leadership, to determine and ensure the implementation of the strategic and financial goals of NZRC. \r\nAlong with governance, the National Board also appoints our Secretary General overseeing the entire operation.",
